From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] clk: qcom: apcs-msm8916: get the PLL from the clock device

The APCS mailbox driver assigns the clock device its clock-controller
child's firmware node when one exists, or reuses the mailbox node for
legacy DTs. Get the PLL input from that clock device so both layouts
work. Looking it up on the mailbox parent misses clocks moved into the
binding's dedicated clock-controller child.

Keep the shared register map on the parent and preserve the existing
clock name. This does not enable the clock driver or CPU frequency scaling.

Base: pem120/linux-msm89x7 a51b91b503307d35902447dd1f90db765372cf3b
Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/apcs-msm8916.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/apcs-msm8916.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/apcs-msm8916.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/apcs-msm8916.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 	a53cc->src_shift = 8;
 	a53cc->parent_map = gpll0_a53cc_map;
 
-	a53cc->pclk = devm_clk_get(parent, NULL);
+	a53cc->pclk = devm_clk_get(dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(a53cc->pclk)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(a53cc->pclk);
 		if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER)
